WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.220
- Your father, obviously, Kirk Douglas,

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.290
everybody loves as well,

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.980
but he passed away before the pandemic.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.710
So, what's the best
advice he ever gave you?

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.130
Because I always get nervous

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.510
about my kids wanting
to be in this industry.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.200
I'm happy for them if they want to do it.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.610
But I imagine he might've
been a little nervous

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.530
'cause he knew all the ins and outs of it.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.310
So did he ever give you any good advice?

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.933
- Yeah, he was nervous.

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:22.539
I think he knows, you know,

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:26.340
we deal with it, high, high unemployment

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.533
in our performance or performers.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.830
Yeah, I guess the best advice he gave me,

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.021
I'll have to clean it up a little bit,

00:00:35.021 --> 00:00:35.854
(everyone laughs)

00:00:35.854 --> 00:00:38.037
but he says, "Look, you gotta do,

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.837
"if you do the best you can,

00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:43.127
"you just know and you walk
away from the best you can.

00:00:43.127 --> 00:00:45.597
"And when you walk away,
you just say (beep) it."

00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:47.760
(everyone laughs)

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.908
(audience applauds)

00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:49.741
- That's awesome.

00:00:49.741 --> 00:00:51.430
- And that was pretty
much it for me, you know?

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.218
So I said just know you gave it your full.

00:00:55.218 --> 00:00:56.051
- Yeah.

00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:58.280
- So he, you know, he was 103.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.180
We lost him last year, February, so,

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.013
- Yeah.

00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:02.846
- it was a good time.

00:01:02.846 --> 00:01:03.679
You're gonna go, it was a good time.

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:05.100
He missed all of that.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.720
And then I just two weeks ago, his wife,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.030
my stepmother, Anne, but
Anne was my stepmother

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.400
for 63 years.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.233
- Wow!

00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:19.140
- So I've known her very well

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.280
and she passed away and I
was very, very fond of her.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.150
Stepparents sometimes, you know, they get

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.207
a bad rap and

00:01:27.207 --> 00:01:28.138
- It can be a thankless job.

00:01:28.138 --> 00:01:30.560
- I'm just...it can be a thankless job.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.007
And, you know, for those stepparents

00:01:33.007 --> 00:01:35.573
and I had a great stepfather too.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.040
And actually the four of them,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.490
my mother and stepfather,
and Kirk and my stepmother,

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.440
they used to get together,
the four of them,

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.560
preferably without the kids,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.976
to have a meal, they got
along really, really well.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:50.809
- What?

00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:51.970
- But I like to put a big plug in there.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.178
Yeah, They got along wonderfully,

00:01:54.178 --> 00:01:55.011
- Wow!

00:01:55.011 --> 00:01:57.240
- wonderfully well, enjoyed
each other's companies

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.687
and got to complain about the kids.

00:01:59.687 --> 00:02:01.047
(audience laughs)

00:02:01.047 --> 00:02:03.040
So that was a good situation.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.053
- Yeah, absolutely.

